Is a UNION-OVER-ANCHORS argument needed, or do DeepenComplete §3+§5 already cover it?
BAD-BIG = non-singleton true orbits that are ENTIRELY bad anchors (the discriminator)
covered-by-§5 = every anchor is GOOD or Aut-RIGID  =>  orbitComplete_of_good_or_trivial

